      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14221848/assets/4c3e53db0b578b306a12711c4e69a0d75b850cb1eecc8d5b0e6df79acc494d7a.png)\n\nA dilation with center $O$ is defined by the function $(x,y)↦(0.2x,0.2y).$  What is the image of the line shown above under the action of this transformation?",
      "worked_solution": "A dilation leaves a line passing through the center of the dilation unchanged.\n\nTherefore, the image ${l}^{′}$ of the line $l$ under the dilation  $(x,y)↦(0.2x,0.2y)$ is the line $l$ itself, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14221848/assets/1ab7188d164a491720d4d9d361abd4c2c76ea2cb09f6edbea3b0790a6281a785.png)",
